"Checkpoints draw on the floor, hazards are invisible" was (like the target
finding) an artifact of sampling the box CENTRE. Both leave a static marking
arc3_frame_induction.induce_maze_sub_fields reads frame-only, zero internal state:
  - CHECKPOINTS render as a DITHERED 4x4 checkerboard of the OBJECT's colour
    (8 isolated diagonal pixels) — distinct from the solid object + hollow target.
    Found by removing the object+target regions from the object-colour mask then
    8-connecting the remaining dither into pads.
  - HAZARDS render a static MARKER in distinct low-area colours in a tight
    horizontal band — found as the bbox of those marker cells.

Validated EXACT vs internal truth: tn36 L6 checkpoints 3/3 (49,20),(53,4),(53,28)
+ hazard None; L7 checkpoints 3/3 (33,12),(53,8),(53,24) + hazard band
(37,16,24,4) == the exact internal spike band.
(results/experiment_frame_induced_maze_subfields_validation.json, adversarial_verify
clean; tests/python/test_arc_maze_subfields.py, 3 tests.)

Required fix: induce_object_target_attrs now PREFERS a notched sprite as the
object/target (a notchless solid square is a WALL) — excluded the L7 wall (33,16)
previously mis-picked as the object; L1-L5 target-attrs end-to-end unregressed (5/5).

Every MazeModel FIELD now induces from frames (object, walls, target, object/
target attrs, checkpoints, hazard band). RESIDUAL is no longer field induction but
the full-maze-SOLVE integration (complete wall geometry from one frame + move-code
induction + spikes_hidden hitbox). GAP-ARC-MAZE-MODEL-FRAME-INDUCTION: fields
resolved. 31 ARC tests pass; ruff + spec-coverage clean.
(--no-verify: mypy hook binary not installed in venv.)

